# OpenRouter MCP Operational Guidelines & Tooling Reference

## Architecture & Transport
- **Server Type**: Remote Model Context Protocol server hosted by OpenRouter (`https://mcp.openrouter.ai/mcp`).
- **Transport**: Remote HTTP/SSE (`application/json, text/event-stream`).
- **Authentication**: OAuth PKCE flow initiated in Cursor via **Settings > MCP > openrouter**.
  - Authorizes a dedicated OpenRouter API key labeled `OpenRouter MCP: <client>`.
  - Configurable expiration (default 7 days) and spend limit (default $10).
  - Can be revoked at any time from the OpenRouter dashboard.

## Purpose & Boundaries
1. **Developer Intelligence & Model Scouting**:
   - Query live model capabilities, parameter availability, and pricing rather than relying on stale model training weights.
   - Compare quality and speed using real-time benchmark indexes (Artificial Analysis, Design Arena ELO).
   - Check account credit balances and inspect past generation costs.
2. **Production Boundary**:
   - The MCP server is a development and inspection assistant for coding agents.
   - Applications and production pipelines should call the OpenRouter REST API (`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`) directly with dedicated production keys, not via the MCP tool.

## Available MCP Tools

| Tool | Scope | Billing | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `list-models` | Read-only | Free | Live catalog search with filters (price, context, modalities, architecture, provider, benchmarks) |
| `get-model` | Read-only | Free | Full details on a single model (parameters, prompt/completion pricing, context window) |
| `list-model-endpoints` | Read-only | Free | Per-provider pricing, latency, throughput, and data privacy policies |
| `list-benchmarks` | Read-only | Free | Third-party benchmarks (Artificial Analysis intelligence/coding/agentic, LMSYS/Design Arena ELO) |
| `list-daily-model-rankings`| Read-only | Free | Trending token volume and most-used models |
| `list-app-rankings` | Read-only | Free | Top applications generating traffic across categories |
| `get-credits` | Read-only | Free | Remaining credit balance on the authenticated account |
| `get-generation` | Read-only | Free | Token breakdown, provider, and exact cost for a generation ID |
| `send-message` | Inference | Billable | Send test prompt to any model to test behavior, tone, or tool-calling |
| `generate-image` | Inference | Billable | Test image generation model directly |
| `search-docs` | Read-only | Free | Query OpenRouter documentation directly |
| `ping` | Diagnostics | Free | Health check verifying endpoint reachability |

## Audit & Verification
To test or audit the OpenRouter MCP connection from the command line:
```bash
python3 scripts/audit_openrouter_mcp.py
```
To validate an active token:
```bash
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-... python3 scripts/audit_openrouter_mcp.py
```
